## FENCES, PARTITION, HOLDS
- **Git:** root history writes only `worktree add -b`, ONE commit, ONE `merge --no-ff`. No `worktree remove`, `fetch`, `push`, `stash`, `reset`, `rebase`, `amend`, `prune`, `gc`, `clean`. In the code repo: `gh api -X GET` only; you clone nothing and edit no file there.
- **HTTP:** `gh api -X GET` to the code repo; the Jira site named in the project's `.env` for the closed-list reads and writes only (python `-I`, token in-process, never printed). No mailbox, no demo, no hosted or production host. No az, ssh, docker, tests, build, deploy, mail, chat, Artifact, Docs, PR, merge of any PR, card or `decision_queue.sh`; no message to any human; no comment or edit on any PR.
- **Yours:** the 11 Jira keys THE LIST holds; root `main` for the one merge; `.tools/wt-b1499-rec`, `records/b1499`; your Step-0 copy, STATUS, `Briefs/2026-11-11_B1499_evidence/`, `.tools/b1499/`. **Read-only:** the register, R209's and R207's STATUS, evidence and `.tools/b1489/scripts/` (copy, never edit). **Not yours:** every other Jira key (PCOMP-77, 75, 15 are C93's; PCOMP-114, 113, 62 are Done by earlier passes), `2_Project_Files` code, `.tools/b1495`, every other seat's tree, open PRs #85, #86, #91.
- **Standing lines:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (above); no message to any human; Jira writes only where THE LIST says; never delete (quarantine); never print a credential; no word added to any user-facing text; `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP.
- **HOLDS:** no deploy and no statement about the hosted state beyond "NOT DEPLOYED" as a repository fact; no ruling of your own (the ruling is quoted; each row's option and recommendation are read from the register by program); no ticket created; no label edited; PCOMP-46, 94, 74, 80, 81, 11 and 52 never move; nothing is sent to the sample-policy reviewer by you (PCOMP-94's send is the project owner's).

